  "question_text": "What is the scientific process of hypothesis testing?",
  "generated_answer": "The scientific process of hypothesis testing begins with a hypothesis that is derived from a broader theory. Researchers design an experiment or observational study that operationally defines the variables and includes an experimental and a control group when possible. The hypothesis is then tested by collecting measurable data; if the results are consistent with the prediction, the hypothesis—and thus the theory—is supported. If the results contradict the prediction, the theory is revised or a new hypothesis is generated. This deductive, falsifiable approach ensures that only hypotheses that can be empirically disproved are considered valid.",
